 HISTORY                                                            76 1451
 -------                                                            76 1451
    This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction         76 1451
    Physics (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University, USA.   76 1451
    The thermal scattering law data for Uranium in Uranium          76 1451
    Carbide was developed using ab initio lattice dynamics          76 1451
    (AILD)[1,2]. Ten temperatures are available in this library.    76 1451
    The Full Law Analysis Scattering System Hub (FLASSH) system     76 1451
    was used to produce File 7 MT = 2, 4 data for Uranium in UC     76 1451
    [3]. MAT=76 and ZA=176 are used for U in UC (natural U,         76 1451
    abundances from [5]). Elemental AWR and cross sections were     76 1451
    computed from ENDF/B-VIII.0 MF=3 MT=2 nuclide evaluations [4]   76 1451
    at 1e-5eV with 12C updated to reflect a mass of exactly 12 amu  76 1451
